; Two secp256k1 backends, deliberately.
;
; mirage-crypto-ec's P256k1.Dsa is fiat-crypto generated, constant time, and is
; the only thing a private key is handed to. mirage-crypto-blockchain's
; Secp256k1 is a plain double-and-add reference implementation carrying a "NOT
; CONSTANT TIME" banner in its own .mli; it is used only for recovery, which
; runs on a signature and a digest that are about to be published anyway.
;
; ocaml-evm's evm-crypto makes exactly this split. Do not collapse it: the
; reference backend also offers sign and sign_recoverable, and calling either
; would put a secret key through non-constant-time scalar multiplication.

(library
 (name tron_crypto)
 (public_name tron-crypto)
 (libraries
  tron-types
  digestif
  mirage-crypto-ec
  mirage-crypto-blockchain
  zarith))
